---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Stainless Steel Wire Mesh (304/316) — Specs, Prices & Anping Factories" description="Stainless steel woven wire mesh: 304 vs 316, mesh sizes 1–635, wire diameter, weight and open area. Source direct from Anping factories.">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8">
    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="flex-1 min-w-0 prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-theme-primary">Stainless Steel Wire Mesh</h1>
      <p class="text-theme-secondary">Stainless steel woven mesh is the workhorse of industrial filtration and screening. Anping factories weave it from 1 mesh (heavy quarry screen) down to 635 mesh (pharmaceutical-grade), in rolls typically 1 m wide × 30 m long.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">304 vs 316</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Ni / Cr</th><th>Corrosion resistance</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>304</td><td>8% Ni, 18% Cr</td><td>Good — indoor & general outdoor</td><td>Filtration, screening, food contact</td></tr>
          <tr><td>316 / 316L</td><td>10–14% Ni, 16–18% Cr + Mo</td><td>Excellent — marine & chemical</td><td>Coastal, chemical processing, pharma</td></tr>
          <tr><td>304 is ~15–20% cheaper than 316</td><td colspan="3" class="text-theme-muted">Unless you need Mo-grade corrosion resistance, 304 is the default.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Common specifications</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Mesh</th><th>Wire (mm)</th><th>Opening (mm)</th><th>Weight (kg/m²)</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>8</td><td>0.7</td><td>2.48</td><td>2.76</td><td>Filter support</td></tr>
          <tr><td>20</td><td>0.4</td><td>0.87</td><td>1.58</td><td>Water filtration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>40</td><td>0.25</td><td>0.39</td><td>0.97</td><td>Oil / liquid filtration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>60</td><td>0.19</td><td>0.23</td><td>0.70</td><td>Fine filtration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100</td><td>0.10</td><td>0.154</td><td>0.49</td><td>Standard filter cloth</td></tr>
          <tr><td>200</td><td>0.05</td><td>0.077</td><td>0.25</td><td>Pharmaceutical</td></tr>
          <tr><td>325</td><td>0.035</td><td>0.043</td><td>0.22</td><td>Lab sieving</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Weights are theoretical plain-weave values. <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">Calculate any spec →</a></p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">What to specify when ordering</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Grade: 304 or 316 (ask for a material test certificate — MTC)</li>
        <li>Mesh count and wire diameter in mm (avoid gauge-only specs)</li>
        <li>Weave: plain, twill (for &gt;100 mesh heavy wire), or Dutch weave</li>
        <li>Roll width and length; edges selvage or cut</li>
        <li>Quantity in m² or kg — factories quote per kg for woven mesh</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Price reference</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Product</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Spec</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Price Range (USD/kg)</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">MOQ</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Lead Time</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">SS304 woven mesh</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20–100 mesh, 0.1–0.4mm wire</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$8–15/kg</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">1 roll / 100m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–25 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">SS316 woven mesh</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">40–200 mesh, 0.05–0.25mm</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$12–22/kg</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20–30 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Dutch weave filter cloth</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">5–40 micron rating</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$25–60/kg</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">25–40 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Ultra-fine 325–635 mesh</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Pharma/lab grade</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$35–80/kg</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">30–45 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-theme-muted mb-6">*Indicative 2025–2026 ranges. Actual pricing depends on wire cost, order volume, weave complexity, and certification requirements. Always request formal quotes.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">FAQ</h2>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How is woven mesh priced?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">By weight (USD/kg) plus weaving complexity. Finer mesh with thin wire costs more per kg because weaving is slower. Dutch weave is the most expensive.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Typical MOQ?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Stock specs: 1 roll. Custom spec: usually 100–500 m². Anping factories are flexible on first orders to win long-term buyers.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How do I verify it's real stainless steel?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Request MTC from the wire rod batch, and do a spot PMI test or magnet check on samples (304 is weakly magnetic after cold drawing — a strong magnet sticking hard suggests low-grade steel).</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What's the difference between plain, twill, and Dutch weave?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary"><strong>Plain weave:</strong> over-under pattern, most common, good for general filtration. <strong>Twill weave:</strong> wires pass over 2+ wires, allows heavier wire in fine mesh, better flow. <strong>Dutch weave:</strong> thick warp + thin weft wires, very fine filtration (1–100 micron), no square openings.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can I get food-grade or pharma certification?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes. Ask for FDA-compliant materials, ISO 9001 factory cert, and third-party test reports (SGS/BV/TÜV). Some factories specialize in pharma mesh with documented traceability.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How do I calculate shipping weight for woven mesh?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Use our <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">weight calculator</a> — enter mesh count, wire diameter, width and length to get kg per roll. For container planning, see the <a href="/tools/container-loading-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">container loading calculator</a>.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What surface treatments are available?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Stainless mesh is usually supplied "as woven" (lightly oil-coated for protection). Options include: degreased/cleaned for food use, passivated for enhanced corrosion resistance, and pre-crimped for structural applications.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="not-prose mt-8 bg-theme-secondary text-white rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Get quotes from Anping stainless mesh factories</p>
        <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block mt-3 accent-bg hover:accent-bg font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Send an inquiry →</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="lg:w-80 shrink-0">
      <div class="sticky top-24 space-y-6">
        <!-- Quick Tools -->
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-theme-accent tracking-widest mb-3">QUICK TOOLS</p>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Calculate & Convert</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Weight Calculator
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/charts/mesh-size-chart/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Mesh Size Chart
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/mesh-count-conversion/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Mesh Count Converter
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/fob-price-calculator/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> FOB Price Calculator
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick Specs -->
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-theme-accent tracking-widest mb-3">QUICK SPECS</p>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Stainless Mesh Standards</h3>
          <dl class="space-y-2 text-xs">
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Mesh Count</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">1–635 mesh</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Wire Diameter</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">0.025–2.0 mm</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Roll Width</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">0.5–2.0 m</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Roll Length</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">10–100 m</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Material</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">SS304 / 316 / 316L</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <dt class="text-theme-muted">Standards</dt>
              <dd class="text-theme-primary">ASTM E2016<br/>ISO 9044<br/>GB/T 5330</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <!-- Related Products -->
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-theme-accent tracking-widest mb-3">RELATED</p>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Related Products</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>
              <a href="/products/welded-wire-mesh/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Welded Wire Mesh
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/products/wire-mesh-fence-panels/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Fence Panels
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/products/gabion-baskets/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Gabion Baskets
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
